{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pulls/509","id":4822940894,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU-508s8AAAABH3g83g","html_url":"https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/509","diff_url":"https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/509.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/509.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/issues/509","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pulls/509/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pulls/509/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/issues/509/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/statuses/7b9c720ecc9f483c383e7cd9c2ab81f06ee5df59","number":509,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Lemma G of #484: clean proof and Lean 4 formalisation of its core","user":{"login":"DreamingOfClouds","id":173691639,"node_id":"U_kgDOClpS9w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173691639?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DreamingOfClouds","html_url":"https://github.com/DreamingOfClouds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DreamingOfClouds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DreamingOfClouds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DreamingOfClouds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DreamingOfClouds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DreamingOfClouds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DreamingOfClouds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DreamingOfClouds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DreamingOfClouds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DreamingOfClouds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"\nThis PR gives Lemma G (entrance gauge: target-side compensation at nonzero frames, labelled targets, chain scatter) a clean,\nself-contained proof and formalises its abstract core in Lean 4.\n\nLemma G is worth +1.80% of complex `b` under no-bank hosting:\n\n| word | complex `b` |\n| --- | --- |\n| Lemma-G-free path (kernel79 only, #500) | 1.310216e-3 |\n| full gauge/kernel word (#496/#500) | 1.333854e-3 |\n\n#484 is not modified. This branch is stacked on #484's head and adds only `research/e8-lemma-g-lean/`.\n\n### What is proved (Lean 4.21.0 + Mathlib v4.21.0, the pin of `formal/lean` on main)\n\n```lean\ntheorem LemmaG.Stream.conj_matrix (T : Λ → M ≃ₗ[K] M) (rec : Λ → Λ → M → M) (es : List (Event ι Λ K))\n    (l : ι → Λ) (h : ι → M) (hrec : RecipesExact T rec es) (hw : WellLabelled es l) (r : ι) :\n    physRun rec es h r = T (labRun es l r) (∑ s, S es r s • (T (l s)).symm (h s))\n```\n\nThe theorem holds for every semiring `K`, every `K`-module `M` and every family of linear automorphisms `T`. Take any stream of relabel/add/scale/copy/clear events that is well labelled and whose relabels execute `T_B T_A⁻¹`. Then for every input it computes\n\n`h_r ↦ T_{λ¹_r}(Σ_s S_rs T_{λ⁰_s}⁻¹ h_s)`,\n\nwhere the non-private columns of `S` are exactly what #484's rational scalar replay computes (`S_rowform`; the replay starts the private copies empty, and their columns drop out on inputs with empty private registers).\n\nThe other Lean results:\n* **Row lemmas** (`row_unit`, `row_pair`). A unit row gives the block `T_{λ¹}T_{λ⁰}⁻¹`; for an entering helper this is the virtual entrance with its wrappers. A paired row gives `T_{λ¹_r}(T_{λ⁰_r}⁻¹h_r + a·T_{λ⁰_s}⁻¹h_s)`.\n* **Schedule** (`emit_spec`, `comp_segment`, `centre_forward`, `centre_backward`), proved for an abstract order with strictly monotone rank and instantiated for the subspaces of F₂⁹.\n  * The compensation segment and the centre phase are well labelled as soon as the partners stay at their frames.\n  * Under (b) and (c), every move is a strict nested ascent (or descent).\n  * Each target ends at `L_t = max ℰ_t`.\n* **Accounting** (`paid_telescopes`). Paid ranks telescope to `rk λ¹ − rk λ⁰` per register.\n* **Bit-side entrance identities** (`Dbit_one_mul`, `Dbit_conj`). `D_I D_P = D_{I−P}`, and conjugation by `diag(g,g)` for `gᵀg = 1`, for every `P`.\n\nAll theorems are general: there is no instance enumeration and no `decide`/`native_decide`. Lean proves the abstract core. The schedule lemmas are an a-priori route that is not instantiated on the emitted stream; the stream itself is checked in Python (below). Combining the Lean core with those checks gives that the data rows are W's and the mass identity `mass(W) − Σ_j dim E_j`. `#print axioms` reports only `propext`, `Classical.choice` and `Quot.sound`. `verify.py` builds the package, scans for `sorry`/`axiom`/`native_decide`, and checks every axiom report.\n\n### What stays checked in Python\n\nThe instance hypotheses on the emitted streams:\n\n| hypothesis | check | result |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| well-labelledness | #484 G0/G2/G3, plus the new `code/check_extended_labels.py` | 0 violations on all four words, both orientations; 3 adapter mutants rejected on every word, 2 wrapper mutants on the wrapper words |\n| exact transition recipes; the adapter/wrapper bridge | #484 I-tr on all 512 columns (recipes are linear circuits); one non-identity adapter per source and per target, all others identities (`check_extended_labels.py`) | 2945/2945 |\n| the scalar identity `S` | #484 replay, all 800 columns | exact |\n| endpoint labels | #484 G4 | 0 violations |\n| accounting | #484 G2/G3/ACC | 0 violations |\n| #433's data-adapter identities | the new `code/check_adapters.py`, every port, all 512 columns, exact | 0 failures on all four words |\n\nWhy the extended-label check: #484 §2.1 left adapters and wrappers outside Lemma C as endpoint operators. Register-wise that is right. Each non-identity adapter and each wrapper is the first or last event on its register, and the adapters that sit mid-stream (headline forward: 550 entry, 672 exit) are all identities. So #484's description was imprecise but harmless. Lemma C as stated still needed an unwritten commutation step. The clean proof reads adapters and wrappers as relabel events of an extended label set (tag × frame), so the theorem covers the complete emitted stream, and the condition is checked directly.\n\nWith these hypotheses checked exhaustively, and Lemma A (#484 I-helper, exhaustive), the end-to-end identity holds **for every input with empty private registers**. #484's `lg_e2e.py` tested it on 814 sampled columns.\n\n`PROOF.md` §5 lists the other clarifications:\n* the relabel-source condition;\n* the inherited facts behind \"every input\" (#433's adapter identities, Lemma A);\n* the minimal label condition;\n* (a)–(d) are accounting-only;\n* explicit side conditions;\n* the kernel updates as an instance of the same emitter.\n\n### Reproduce\n\n```sh\npython3 research/e8-lemma-g-lean/verify.py                                   # Lean only: cache get + build + axioms\npython3 research/e8-lemma-g-lean/verify.py --instances /abs/out/of/484/verify # plus the instance checks (numpy)\n```\n\n### Credits\n\n* #425 (Zhihao Chen): the common-frame conjugation lemma and scalar interface.\n* #458 (chafreaky): the one-helper rule and paid wrappers.\n* #471 (Dugongue): the virtual entrance and complete-invocation normalisation.\n* #484 (DreamingOfClouds): the gauge construction, Lemma G and its Python check stage.\n* `formal/lean` on main: the Lean toolchain and Mathlib pin.\n* #487/#488 (jamesyc): the standalone Lean package layout and axiom reporting.\n\nPrepared by DreamingOfClouds with Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), via Claude Code.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"acti